1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:04,500
They are part of a new and developing arsenal.

2
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:06,000
Please wait.

3
00:00:06,001 --> 00:00:10,000
Countermeasures designed to answer the looming threat of terror

4
00:00:10,001 --> 00:00:12,000
against corporate targets.

5
00:00:12,001 --> 00:00:15,000
Threats that cannot be specified or even seen

6
00:00:15,001 --> 00:00:17,000
until the damage has begun.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,540
They are breathtaking structures, titans that can rise more than 100 stories from the ground

8
00:00:39,541 --> 00:00:42,431
and contain upwards of a million square feet.

9
00:00:42,432 --> 00:00:45,580
Among the greatest monuments to wealth, commerce,

10
00:00:45,581 --> 00:00:50,176
and capitalism, they are the symbol of corporate America.

11
00:00:50,177 --> 00:00:53,160
Ever since the first skyscrapers were

12
00:00:53,161 --> 00:00:59,320
erected in the 1930s, these towers were heralded as efficient and centralized places to concentrate

13
00:00:59,321 --> 00:01:02,720
and conduct business in the modern world.

14
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:06,220
But in the days following 9-11, corporate high-rise buildings

15
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:09,320
everywhere emerged in the public eye for another reason,

16
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:14,160
as a prime target for large-scale terrorist attack.

17
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:17,180
To defend these giants and the people who work in them,

18
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,580
an army of scientists, engineers, and security advisors

19
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:24,580
have begun a vital mission, to develop the web of technologies

20
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,480
that will come together to make corporate America safe

21
00:01:27,481 --> 00:01:29,480
safe from terrorist attack.

22
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:36,080
Some rely on complex biological sensors,

23
00:01:36,081 --> 00:01:40,220
marvels that can sniff out traces of anthrax or explosives

24
00:01:40,221 --> 00:01:43,020
and give warning in time to save lives.

25
00:01:43,021 --> 00:01:48,640
Others use artificial intelligence to recognize the face of terror

26
00:01:48,641 --> 00:01:52,280
from a database of millions and sound the alarm.

27
00:01:52,281 --> 00:01:56,280
Some rely on brute strength and remarkable engineering

28
00:01:56,281 --> 00:02:01,080
to make sensitive targets safe from attack,

29
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,180
at the moment it counts.

30
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:10,520
When all else fails, there are extreme life-saving measures,

31
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:13,840
a newly developed technology that can seek out radiation

32
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:16,040
before an attack with a dirty bomb.

33
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,340
Which tells me there's something radioactive here.

34
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,680
And a parachute designed to help victims

35
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,280
survive the unthinkable.

36
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:32,780
Security experts list them among the soft targets, places

37
00:02:32,781 --> 00:02:35,280
vulnerable to harm from many angles.

38
00:02:35,281 --> 00:02:38,280
This is because, to a terrorist cell,

39
00:02:38,281 --> 00:02:41,280
any area of a high-rise building holds the potential

40
00:02:41,281 --> 00:02:44,280
to be exploited in an attack.

41
00:02:44,281 --> 00:02:47,280
Because of car or truck bombs, like those used in attacks

42
00:02:47,281 --> 00:02:50,280
on foreign embassies, the Federal Building in Oklahoma

43
00:02:50,281 --> 00:02:53,280
City, and even the World Trade Center in 1990,

44
00:02:53,281 --> 00:02:56,580
and even the World Trade Center in 1993,

45
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:00,320
most security consultants agree that protecting a high rise

46
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,220
from terrorists starts on the ground floor.

47
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:20,000
If an 18-wheeler fully loaded was to hit or strike one

48
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,440
of our vehicle barriers, the kinetic energy

49
00:03:22,441 --> 00:03:25,540
The kinetic energy of the vehicle would be absorbed

50
00:03:25,541 --> 00:03:28,280
by the structure of our barrier and then down

51
00:03:28,281 --> 00:03:30,380
into the foundation or the soil.

52
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:35,040
This is the high-tech world where potential truck bombs

53
00:03:35,041 --> 00:03:39,100
are reduced to terms like mass, speed, and kinetic energy,

54
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:42,000
where they are destroyed in a violent crash

55
00:03:42,001 --> 00:03:44,520
which spares the target but not the driver.

56
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,800
It can be a pickup truck.

57
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:49,140
It can be an 18-wheeler.

58
00:03:49,141 --> 00:03:52,180
It can be a heavily loaded fuel truck.

59
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,700
we can stop them effectively if they're deployed properly.

60
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:01,120
The engineers behind this brand of brute strength

61
00:04:01,121 --> 00:04:03,280
are at California's Delta Scientific,

62
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,720
a little-known brand name that's at work

63
00:04:05,721 --> 00:04:08,280
in some of the most high-profile targets in the world.

64
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:12,560
Some of the places which we feel free to speak about

65
00:04:12,561 --> 00:04:14,060
are the Pentagon.

66
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:18,600
Nearly every building on Capitol Hill has our equipment.

67
00:04:18,601 --> 00:04:22,900
Although they cannot disclose the other locations,

68
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,240
delta barriers like this one, the IP5000,

69
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:29,040
are protecting some of the tallest corporate skyscrapers

70
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:29,940
in America.

71
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,460
Especially after the 9-11 attack,

72
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:39,260
there have been many applications of our vehicle

73
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,260
barricades to protect high rise buildings,

74
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:45,660
as this is an obvious, established target.

75
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,600
Each barricade installation starts

76
00:04:48,601 --> 00:04:50,340
with a risk analysis.

77
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:53,180
The goal is to stop the truck bomb as far away

78
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,800
from the protected structure as possible

79
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:59,420
to minimize damage in case of explosion.

80
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:01,280
To safeguard a high-rise building,

81
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,420
you would look at the threat, in other words,

82
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:07,120
the size and speed a vehicle could approach the building,

83
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:10,060
and then look at where you could place the barricades

84
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:14,320
and to allow access control.

85
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:16,100
These steel structures are massive

86
00:05:16,101 --> 00:05:19,240
and can weigh upwards of 11,000 pounds.

87
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:22,280
But the engineers here know that a 15,000 pound truck

88
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:25,740
traveling at 50 miles per hour will strike its target

89
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:29,720
with more than a million pounds of force.

90
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,220
For the amount of kinetic energy that they're stopping,

91
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,780
they're actually very lightweight structures.

92
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:41,060
And the physics to conduct the flow of kinetic energy

93
00:05:41,061 --> 00:05:47,560
into foundations away from the vehicle is tremendous.

94
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,900
The technology behind these super barriers

95
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,740
promises that each one will stop a speeding truck

96
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,940
bomb dead in its tracks.

97
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,780
But in the life and death world of counterterrorism,

98
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:00,440
promises are not enough.

99
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:03,880
The testing process is the proof of the design.

100
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:08,720
The way we test a barricade is that we put it into as real

101
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:10,420
a situation as possible.

102
00:06:10,421 --> 00:06:14,860
We'll actually dig a hole, pour a standard foundation,

103
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:19,280
have a fully operating barricade at the end of a long runway.

104
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,980
We then take an attacking vehicle.

105
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,860
And there's nothing that is more thrilling and unnerving to us

106
00:06:27,861 --> 00:06:32,240
to see this vehicle slowly start accelerating faster and faster and faster

107
00:06:32,241 --> 00:06:35,360
as it draws nearer to the vehicle barrier.

108
00:06:35,361 --> 00:06:42,360
You see it collide with a very resounding sound.

109
00:06:42,361 --> 00:06:44,360
There's immediate damage to the truck,

110
00:06:44,361 --> 00:06:48,360
which usually means that the engine has been displaced from

111
00:06:48,361 --> 00:06:51,360
the frame, pushed back into the cab,

112
00:06:51,361 --> 00:06:56,360
and so the energy is dissipated in heat, sound, and fury.

113
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:03,360
The moment of truth lasts just 2 tenths of a second,

114
00:07:03,361 --> 00:07:04,260
of a second.

115
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,600
But when the dust settles, the attacking truck

116
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:10,400
has been completely destroyed and its driver presumed dead.

117
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:13,840
In a real-life scenario, a catastrophic terrorist attack

118
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:15,040
would have just been thwarted.

119
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,340
In the event an unprotected building

120
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:23,040
gets warning that it might be in imminent danger of attack,

121
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,980
a portable version of the Delta Barrier

122
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,680
can be set up in 15 minutes.

123
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:32,160
Tests prove that this machine has the same stopping power

124
00:07:32,161 --> 00:07:33,560
as its big brothers.

125
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,800
This barricade is the one that was crash test.

126
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:36,800
This is the very unit.

127
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:44,740
The solid steel stopping plate of the MP5000

128
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,980
weighs 3,000 pounds.

129
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:50,620
Close inspection reveals no damage to this portable barrier

130
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,940
save for a small nick.

131
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,720
The truck was completely destroyed.

132
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:58,120
The driver most likely would have been killed.

133
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:02,160
It's still ready to go, still ready to protect you.

134
00:08:02,161 --> 00:08:05,760
But solid steel is not the only defense a corporation can use

135
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,760
to protect its ground floor from a terrorist car bomb.

136
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,340
At the laboratory and test site of computer recognition systems

137
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:18,040
in Cambridge, Massachusetts, another technology

138
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:21,540
is taking shape that promises to quickly identify a vehicle

139
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,740
that might be carrying a bomb.

140
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:25,920
The system can prevent a high-rise building

141
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:27,820
or any building from coming under terrorist attack

142
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:30,780
by only allowing known drivers and permitted drivers

143
00:08:30,781 --> 00:08:32,680
to the building.

144
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:37,720
The $150,000 CRS Vista uses video cameras, sensors,

145
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:41,620
and computers to match arriving cars against vehicles

146
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,720
in its database.

147
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:46,820
It also checks to see if an incoming vehicle weighs more

148
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:52,240
than it should, a warning sign that a bomb might be on board.

149
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:54,880
Vista begins to work as soon as a vehicle approaches

150
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:57,540
its rectangular white sensor.

151
00:08:57,541 --> 00:09:00,440
The sensor received radio frequency identification,

152
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:02,760
or RFID for short.

153
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:08,040
Each vehicle has an RFID transponder in the windshield.

154
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:13,260
And this tag associates the vehicle and the person in the vehicle

155
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:15,160
with the database.

156
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:17,900
The database has a photograph of the individual.

157
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,700
It's a photograph of the vehicle.

158
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:22,580
It's got the weight per axle of the vehicle,

159
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:25,500
the gross vehicle weight, and a record of the license plate.

160
00:09:25,501 --> 00:09:29,500
Proprietary software compares the image of the license plate,

161
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:32,500
the driver, and the vehicle with the information stored

162
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,500
in the database.

163
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:38,540
Any deviation alerts security personnel to possible danger,

164
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:43,660
before the car and a possible intruder with a bomb gets inside.

165
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:48,760
Here we have what the actual axle weight was

166
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,660
and what the axle weight should be for both axles.

167
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:54,660
In the event that this was, this car was of a weight

168
00:09:54,661 --> 00:09:56,460
or these license plates not match,

169
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,900
we would flash an alarm.

170
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,300
But stopping a possible car bomb outside

171
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:04,640
is only one layer of protection in the complex matrix

172
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:07,100
of anti-terror technology being developed

173
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,100
to protect the corporate high-rise building from attack.

174
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:23,660
Controlling the entry of people into a corporate high-rise

175
00:10:23,661 --> 00:10:26,400
is crucial to preventing a terrorist attack.

176
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,160
But given the hundreds of thousands

177
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,960
who may enter the building each day,

178
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:33,900
monitoring each one is a daunting task.

179
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,180
Today, technologies are emerging that tirelessly work

180
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,640
to guard a building's entrance and perimeter

181
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,280
to warn of intruders before they get inside.

182
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:51,160
This is video surveillance that can think.

183
00:10:51,161 --> 00:10:53,860
It represents the union of applied mathematics,

184
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:57,200
computer science, and electrical engineering.

185
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:59,000
In the world of corporate security,

186
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:01,500
it is a new breed of watchdog.

187
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:05,200
Its designer calls it Video IQ.

188
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,600
The big picture of Video IQ is pretty simple.

189
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:10,620
It's an automated video surveillance system

190
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:13,520
that detects the presence of humans, all weather, day,

191
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:15,020
night.

192
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:17,820
The system is programmed to distinguish between people

193
00:11:17,821 --> 00:11:21,160
and other moving images like cars, shadows, and trees.

194
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,160
In a typical security application,

195
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:30,560
the camera's field of view is quite a bit wider

196
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,860
than the region that you're actually interested in.

197
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:36,380
So in this case, we have the camera up here looking out

198
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:39,980
over public areas and the edge of our property.

199
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,380
People in the public area is perfectly OK.

200
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,380
When they step into our own property,

201
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,580
the area that we want under surveillance,

202
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,620
we want our system to alert us.

203
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,680
Is it a vehicle?

204
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:50,820
Is it a person?

205
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:53,720
So when you saw my car come through the region of interest,

206
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:56,620
when it nudged through, yellow box on the car.

207
00:11:56,720 --> 00:12:00,060
As soon as I step out, red box on me.

208
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,400
The underlying foundation

209
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,400
is the system's ability to learn.

210
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,060
At its heart is a neural network that allows the machine

211
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:09,100
to define images, such as a human or a vehicle,

212
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,100
and decide which one to watch.

213
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:15,340
Three basic components that rely on this cool technology.

214
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:19,940
One is the detector, and that essentially, if you will,

215
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:23,140
parses the foreground action objects that are of interest

216
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,980
from the dynamic background.

217
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,580
The second component is called the tracker.

218
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:31,080
It scans the scene frame by frame,

219
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:33,700
looking for what it calls action objects

220
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:37,000
and keeps track of anything that moves.

221
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:39,300
The third component is the classifier,

222
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:43,500
and that's the real brain that distinguishes the humans

223
00:12:43,501 --> 00:12:45,640
from non-human action objects.

224
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:49,440
And then we zero in on the humans and keep track of them.

225
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:52,040
It takes less than a second for the system's neural net

226
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:56,240
to distinguish a human moving in its field of view.

227
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:58,620
The upper right image here shows you

228
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,980
a typical response to the system when people enter

229
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,880
the field of view.

230
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,180
Here comes a person.

231
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:06,760
And as soon as he's in the full field of view,

232
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:09,520
he's detected as a person and bounded with a red box.

233
00:13:09,521 --> 00:13:17,020
Much like a human brain, Video IQ actually thinks in abstraction.

234
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:19,600
This is its mind's eye.

235
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,140
Abstractly, you can see on the left here,

236
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:25,040
in the center of the image, a pair of people.

237
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,400
It's very abstract.

238
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:29,580
Just below it on the left, you see now an individual person.

239
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:32,980
On the right, opposite that abstract individual person,

240
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:35,040
you see a notion of possibly a vehicle.

241
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:37,040
And then finally here on the left,

242
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:38,040
a vehicle.

243
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:40,080
And then finally here on the lower left,

244
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:43,640
you see what is clearly an abstract representation

245
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:46,580
of a vehicle.

246
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,780
While this system uses abstract reasoning

247
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:51,460
to distinguish people from objects,

248
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:54,260
another science, biometrics, can enhance security

249
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:57,860
by distinguishing people from each other.

250
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,960
The art of positively identifying people

251
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:03,100
by their physical characteristics is not new.

252
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,640
100 years ago, prison inmates were identified

253
00:14:05,641 --> 00:14:08,980
an arcane practice called the Bertillion system.

254
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,940
Technicians painstakingly collected

255
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,380
detailed body measurements of their subject

256
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,680
and combined them into an identity profile.

257
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:20,380
That system gave way to the familiar sciences of photography

258
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,280
and fingerprinting.

259
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,500
Today, a process called live scanning

260
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,740
allows electronic fingerprints to be collected and compared

261
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:34,440
instantly to a database of known criminals and terrorists.

262
00:14:34,441 --> 00:14:37,480
But the state of the art in biometric identification

263
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:41,580
has evolved into the 21st century.

264
