353
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:27,640
Wait for moving life.

354
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:30,740
Try to carry a bomb into some well-protected corporate

355
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:33,440
buildings, and you'll come face to face with this.

356
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,760
Enter.

357
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:37,360
Air pumpers on.

358
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:40,160
It's called the ion track entry scan.

359
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:43,100
The entry scan explosives and narcotics trace detector

360
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:46,700
works on the idea that when somebody has explosives

361
00:19:46,701 --> 00:19:49,100
explosives or narcotics strapped to their body,

362
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:52,740
or for that matter, come into contact with these substances,

363
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:56,040
it can detect these trace amounts or microscopic amounts

364
00:19:56,140 --> 00:19:58,940
of substances on the person.

365
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:02,520
The portal starts to work as soon as a subject steps inside.

366
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:05,280
The puffs of air that hit me were actually releasing

367
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:08,920
particles and vapors that maybe contaminated onto my clothes

368
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:11,660
to actually carry them upwards.

369
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:15,760
The $125,000 ion track system relies

370
00:20:15,761 --> 00:20:19,760
of spectrometry to sniff out traces of explosives,

371
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:22,900
even the few molecules, that are left behind

372
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,800
in a suicide bomber's hair, clothing, or hands

373
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:28,700
after explosives are handled.

374
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:31,800
The entry scan is extremely sensitive down

375
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,420
to the nanogram level.

376
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:35,320
And if you think about what is a nanogram,

377
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:37,420
it's 1 billionth of a gram.

378
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:39,620
The entry scan sample collection system

379
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,320
takes advantage of a natural airflow phenomenon

380
00:20:42,321 --> 00:20:45,360
called the human convection plume.

381
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:48,500
It flows upward around the body and carries vapors

382
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,820
and particles up with it.

383
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,840
Once the subject steps inside, their air sample

384
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:58,700
rises into a collection chamber at the top of the machine.

385
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,880
Next, the molecules in the chamber

386
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:03,640
