447
00:24:24,820 --> 00:24:27,060
Although they are a necessity for waste management,

448
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:29,360
they are also an extremely soft target

449
00:24:29,361 --> 00:24:33,480
which can easily conceal an explosive device planted by a terrorist.

450
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:39,300
The trash can might even heighten the attack

451
00:24:39,301 --> 00:24:41,200
because when the bomb is detonated,

452
00:24:41,201 --> 00:24:45,420
the can itself will add shrapnel and fragmentation to the blast area.

453
00:24:46,540 --> 00:24:48,620
To counter this very real threat,

454
00:24:48,621 --> 00:24:51,560
New York's American Innovations has engineered a sort of trash

455
00:24:51,660 --> 00:24:56,620
can on steroids, the bomb-resistant waste receptacle.

456
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:58,860
As this test video shows, it is designed

457
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:01,660
to contain an explosion and direct the resulting blast

458
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:04,240
