673
00:36:04,640 --> 00:36:06,900
Moti Emek is chief technology consultant

674
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,180
at Old Castle R. Paul Glass.

675
00:36:09,181 --> 00:36:13,880
What we have here is a window that was demonstrated

676
00:36:13,980 --> 00:36:15,980
in a real blast event.

677
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:18,820
Now, this specific window was exposed

678
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:24,860
to a charge of 50 pounds of TNT at a standoff of 30 feet.

679
00:36:24,960 --> 00:36:27,000
The windows aren't designed to look pretty

680
00:36:27,100 --> 00:36:28,160
after an explosion.

681
00:36:28,260 --> 00:36:31,800
Their purpose is singular, to protect the people inside.

682
00:36:31,900 --> 00:36:33,400
What's special about this glass

683
00:36:33,500 --> 00:36:36,300
is that it's made of two layers of glass

684
00:36:36,301 --> 00:36:40,880
of glass with an interlayer of very resilient film.

685
00:36:40,980 --> 00:36:43,140
When subjected to the force of a blast,

686
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:45,300
the windows shatter immediately.

687
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:49,740
But the fragments remained attached

688
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,740
to the interlayer of film.

689
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:55,280
And the whole fabric of fragments of glass with the film

690
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:58,820
will start to balloon in the protected area.

