00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:04,520
Since the glass and the frame creates together a system,

692
00:37:04,521 --> 00:37:08,600
The bonding of the glass to the frame is very special,

693
00:37:08,700 --> 00:37:14,060
and it absorbs some of the blast energy.

694
00:37:14,160 --> 00:37:16,640
Using scenarios that combine a blast's force

695
00:37:16,740 --> 00:37:20,040
and its distance from a building, the Old Castle R. Paul

696
00:37:20,140 --> 00:37:23,100
engineers can design windows to protect against an array

697
00:37:23,200 --> 00:37:26,500
of terrorist threats.

698
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:29,120
This window survived the relatively small charge

699
00:37:29,220 --> 00:37:32,420
that might be delivered in a suitcase bomb at close range.

700
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:40,520
Window number 1810 survived the blast from 220 pounds of TNT,

701
00:37:40,521 --> 00:37:43,520
about the size of a terrorist car bomb.

702
00:37:43,521 --> 00:37:47,520
The next scenario is that the guy comes not with his own car,

703
00:37:47,521 --> 00:37:51,520
but with a little truck, like 5,000 pounds,

704
00:37:51,521 --> 00:37:54,520
like what we had in Oklahoma City.

