00:39:00,681 --> 00:39:05,580
have been protected from the devastating bomb blast.

728
00:39:05,680 --> 00:39:07,820
But in the event prevention fails,

729
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:10,320
breakthrough developments on a familiar technology

730
00:39:10,420 --> 00:39:13,620
may provide a fast way to get out of harm's way.

731
00:39:18,640 --> 00:39:20,540
In the days following September 11th,

732
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:23,540
Americans began to reevaluate all that is supposed

733
00:39:23,640 --> 00:39:25,340
to keep us safe.

734
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:26,840
From the chilling memory of workers

735
00:39:26,940 --> 00:39:29,940
leaping from the upper floors of the World Trade Center,

736
00:39:29,941 --> 00:39:31,980
A team of parachute designers was inspired

737
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:36,280
to create a last resort method to evacuate a burning high rise.

738
00:39:36,380 --> 00:39:38,280
It's called the evacu-chute.

739
00:39:44,380 --> 00:39:48,300
I believe that a lot of people that were trapped in 9-11

740
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:51,900
would have been able to use our evacu-chute system successfully

741
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:53,600
to be able to get out of the building.

742
00:39:53,700 --> 00:39:55,540
It is the first of its kind to address

743
00:39:55,640 --> 00:39:57,900
the growing demand for personal parachutes

744
00:39:57,901 --> 00:40:00,700
among high-rise workers who fear that the unthinkable

745
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:03,800
could happen again.

746
00:40:03,900 --> 00:40:06,440
It is designed for evacuation from a minimum height

747
00:40:06,540 --> 00:40:10,540
of 15 stories, or 130 feet above the ground,

748
00:40:10,640 --> 00:40:12,640
and can be ready for use in less than a minute.

749
00:40:15,460 --> 00:40:17,460
It's very straightforward and simple.

750
00:40:17,560 --> 00:40:22,560
You have three main buckles, main points, your two leg,

751
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:24,160
and your one center.

752
00:40:24,161 --> 00:40:30,200
And what you have here is the static line.

753
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:35,340
And what the individual does is they pull out

754
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:37,080
until they see the red string.

755
00:40:37,180 --> 00:40:41,940
When they see the red string, they don't pull any further.

756
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:43,840
The static line makes the evacu-shoot

757
00:40:43,940 --> 00:40:45,540
work automatically.

758
00:40:45,640 --> 00:40:48,280
Before jumping, the fireproof Kevlar strap

759
00:40:48,380 --> 00:40:51,760
is hooked to a fixed object or wall bracket.

760
00:40:51,761 --> 00:40:55,000
Once that is in place, all the evacuee has to do

761
00:40:55,100 --> 00:40:58,500
is jump feet first and hands free.

762
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:01,600
Everything else is done automatically.

763
00:41:01,700 --> 00:41:03,800
Once in the air, the Kevlar line

764
00:41:03,900 --> 00:41:06,700
acts like a ripcord to deploy the parachute canopy

765
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:09,220
in less than two seconds.

766
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:13,420
It's impossible to have people jumping from a building

767
00:41:13,520 --> 00:41:15,620
deploying the parachute, especially people that

768
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:18,020
have no parachute experience.

769
00:41:18,120 --> 00:41:21,520
Static line, what that ensures is that

770
00:41:21,521 --> 00:41:25,220
that the parachute opens correctly every time,

771
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:29,560
and it's the only fail-safe way that we can make sure

772
00:41:29,660 --> 00:41:33,860
that that deployment is done properly.

773
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:36,360
More cutting-edge design is evident in the parachute's

774
00:41:36,460 --> 00:41:38,160
nylon canopy.

775
00:41:38,260 --> 00:41:41,780
It scoops the air that fills it into the shape of a cone.

776
00:41:41,880 --> 00:41:44,880
This airflow guides the evacuee away from the flames

777
00:41:44,980 --> 00:41:48,280
of a burning building at a 45-degree angle of descent.

778
00:41:48,281 --> 00:41:53,780
The 45-degree angle makes it a lot easier when you do touch down

779
00:41:53,781 --> 00:41:56,920
versus falling straight down at a 90-degree angle.

780
00:41:56,921 --> 00:42:00,980
You're actually able to absorb a little bit more of the shock

781
00:42:00,981 --> 00:42:03,740
of the landing based on that 45-degree angle.

782
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:07,280
Although few people have actually jumped with an evacu-shoot,

783
00:42:07,820 --> 00:42:10,340
the company's president has taken a test flight.

784
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,700
And I'm not a professional parachute,

785
00:42:12,701 --> 00:42:16,540
so to me, it felt comfortable.

